      "papers": [],
      "scope": "Defined-access owner certificate. Payload words are relaxed atomics between release fences; the reader installs them only after acquire fences and a matching even seq. CURRENT_HOLDER is the snapshot rT == rSeen and obsP == 2. A saved CURRENT is not required to stay live. The returned record carries the interrupt-site coverage bound. An uninstrumented acquire does not write the certificate. Negative controls: a plain in-window read, a sticky live reading of CURRENT, ABSENT or HISTORICAL treated as lock-free, and a HISTORICAL snapshot relabeled CURRENT. This is not the failed a00de3f assertion and not the plain-seqlock campaign. Seq wrap, fault preservation, and native admission are outside this check."
    },
    {
      "id": "barrier_local_winner",
      "mode": "characterization",
      "invariants": ["barrierImpl"],
      "temporal": "completion",
      "protocolInitializers": {"barrierImpl": "initProtocol"},
